3, -0.007059706375002861, -0.00781998224556446, 0.006261096801608801, 0.006778595969080925, -0.029031045734882355, -0.001158782048150897, -0.00764109380543232, 0.018336068838834763, -0.0019070790149271488, 0.024558832868933678, 0.020239954814314842, 0.010631087236106396, 0.013978857547044754, -0.010266921482980251, -0.021888284012675285, -0.0040888795629143715, 0.012509415857493877, 0.014387745410203934, 0.006574151571840048, 0.008893312886357307, 0.012841637246310711, -0.02278272621333599, 0.01355719193816185, -0.002994784852489829, 0.01213886123150587, -0.015908297151327133, 0.032021038234233856, 0.016904961317777634, 0.002938882214948535, -0.02731882780790329, 0.012988581322133541, -0.025657719001173973, 0.021389951929450035, -0.01020303275436163, -0.016406629234552383, 0.016853850334882736, 0.020022733137011528, 0.0005007280269637704, -0.02328105829656124, -0.016470517963171005]], "input": ["COKER F:", "RMN HIPOFISARIA:La RMN hipofisaria es un procedimiento diagnóstico esencial que se utiliza para evaluar diversas condiciones relacionadas con la glándula pituitaria. Este tipo de resonancia magnética es especialmente recomendado para niños que presentan pubertad precoz central, particularmente en aquellos menores de 9 años. Además, la RMN hipofisaria es una técnica de imagen eficaz para detectar adenomas corticotropos en pacientes que tienen sospechas de enfermedad de Cushing. En resumen, la RMN hipofisaria es una herramienta clave en la evaluación de trastornos endocrinos, proporcionando información valiosa para el diagnóstico y tratamiento de estas condiciones.", "TAC:TAC, or Tomografía Axial Computarizada, is a diagnostic imaging procedure widely utilized in medical diagnostics to visualize internal structures of the body. This imaging technique, also known as computed tomography (CT), is particularly effective in identifying tumors and other abnormalities across various organs. It is commonly employed to detect lung tumors, pheochromocytomas, and adrenal nodules, among other conditions.\n\nThe TAC provides detailed images that assist in diagnosing and monitoring the progression of diseases, including the evaluation of medullary thyroid carcinoma and the assessment of lesions over time. It has been noted that while TAC is a valuable tool for detecting tumors, it may be less sensitive than magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) for certain conditions, such as corticotroph adenomas.\n\nIn specific cases, TAC has been used to confirm the dilation of the Wirsung duct and to study irregularities in the pancreatic process. Additionally, it is recommended for evaluating extensive cervical involvement in patients with medullary thyroid carcinoma. Overall, TAC is an essential imaging modality in the medical field, often used in conjunction with other imaging methods to enhance diagnostic accuracy.", "CATETERISMO DE SENOS PETROSOS:The \"CATETERISMO DE SENOS PETROSOS\" is a medical procedure employed to assess the hypersecretion of adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH) produced by the pituitary gland, particularly in cases where magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) fails to identify a tumor. This procedure, known as petrosal sinus sampling, is specifically utilized to measure ACTH levels, aiding in the differentiation of the source of ACTH in patients diagnosed with Cushing's syndrome.", "NIEMAN LK:Nieman LK is a prominent medical professional and author recognized for his extensive contributions to the literature on Cushing's syndrome, including its epidemiology, diagnosis, and treatment. He has authored multiple guidelines and literature reviews that address various aspects of the syndrome, including the establishment of its causes and clinical manifestations. Nieman LK is frequently cited in references related to Cushing's syndrome, highlighting his significant role in advancing the understanding and management of this condition. His work encompasses a comprehensive examination of hypercortisolism and its implications, making him a key figure in the field.", "LACROIX A:LACROIX A is an editor and author recognized in the literature concerning both the syndrome of Cushing and the treatment of adrenocortical carcinoma. This individual is cited in various references related to these medical topics, highlighting their contributions to the understanding and management of these conditions.", "KETOCONAZOL:KETOCONAZOL is a medication primarily used in the treatment of Cushing's syndrome. It functions by inhibiting the production of cortisol in the adrenal glands, effectively addressing the hormonal imbalances associated with this condition. Ketoconazole works by inhibiting several enzymes involved in steroidogenesis, which further supports its role in managing elevated cortisol levels.", "METIRAPONA:Metirapona is a medication that functions as an inhibitor of adrenal steroidogenesis, specifically targeting the enzyme 11-β-hydroxylase. This action effectively reduces cortisol production, making metirapona a valuable treatment option for individuals suffering from Cushing's syndrome.", "PASIREÓTIDA:El pasireótida es un fármaco que actúa directamente sobre la secreción de ACTH hipofisaria y se utiliza en el tratamiento del síndrome de Cushing.", "MIFEPRISTONA:Mifepristona, también conocida como mifepristone, es un antagonista de los receptores de progesterona que, en dosis elevadas, también actúa como un antagonista de los receptores de glucocorticoides. Se utiliza en el tratamiento del síndrome de Cushing, una condición caracterizada por la sobreproducción de cortisol. Su capacidad para bloquear estos receptores la convierte en una opción terapéutica importante en el manejo de esta enfermedad.", "PASIREOTIDA:Pasireotida is a novel somatostatin analog characterized by its high affinity for multiple somatostatin receptors. It is primarily utilized in the treatment of Cushing's syndrome. The mechanism of action of Pasireotida involves its effect at the pituitary level, where it reduces the secretion of adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH).", "TAC DE CUERPO ENTERO:Whole-body CT scan is a diagnostic imaging technique used to detect tumors in the body.", "RMN DE CUERPO ENTERO:Whole-body MRI is a diagnostic imaging technique that provides detailed images of the body's internal structures.", "PET:PET, or positron emission tomography, is an advanced imaging technique that is particularly sensitive for diagnosing metastases of malignant paragangliomas, making it a valuable tool in oncology. This imaging test provides insights into how tissues and organs are functioning, which is crucial for cancer diagnosis. Overall, PET is recognized for its effectiveness in detecting and assessing various types of cancer, enhancing the ability to monitor disease progression and treatment response.", "ÁLVAREZ SAN MARTÍN RM:Álvarez San Martín RM is an author of a manual on endocrinology and nutrition.", "URIOSTE FONDO A:Urioste Fondo A is an author of a manual on endocrinology and nutrition."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}